# Implementation Plan - Region-Aware Email Open and Click Tracking

We will design a tracking mechanism for email views (opens) and link clicks that behaves dynamically based on the target **Region** of each Campaign. This ensures compliance with local laws (such as GDPR in Europe, CAN-SPAM/CCPA in the US, DPDPA in India, PDPA in APAC, and PDPL in the Middle East).

---

## Regional Compliance Overview

Here is how tracking will be governed across different campaign target regions:

| Region | Regulatory Body / Law | Tracking Allowance | Implementation Strategy |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **United States** | CAN-SPAM, CCPA/CPRA | Fully allowed | Standard 1x1 tracking pixel and URL redirection. Requires a clear unsubscribe link in all emails. |
| **Europe** | GDPR, ePrivacy Directive | Restricted (Requires Consent/Legitimate Interest) | Tracking is permitted but we must ensure data privacy. We will allow campaign-level toggle or opt-out, and log tracking securely with the ability to delete/anonymize upon request. |
| **India** | DPDPA (2023) | Restricted (Notice & Consent) | Requires clear privacy notices. Tracking will be logged, but the recipient must have a clear option to unsubscribe and access their data. |
| **APAC** | Singapore (PDPA), Australia (Privacy Act) | Notification/Consent Required | Requires transparent disclosure of tracking. Opt-out (unsubscribe) must be honored immediately. |
| **Middle East** | UAE (PDPL), Saudi Arabia (PDPL) | Consent Required | Requires consent or valid grounds. Redirection and pixel loads will be logged responsibly. |

